From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libgcc: FDPIC dl_phdr_info starts with a load map

On FRV and Blackfin FDPIC, uClibc's struct dl_phdr_info begins with a
struct elf32_fdpic_loadaddr, not an address, as _Unwind_IteratePhdrCallback's
load_base already has it.  ext_dl_phdr_info, the callback's view of the
extended fields, declared an address, so it read dlpi_adds and dlpi_subs
from the wrong words and could keep a stale FDE cache after a dlopen or
dlclose.  Declare the load map there too.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>

diff --git a/libgcc/unwind-dw2-fde-dip.c b/libgcc/unwind-dw2-fde-dip.c
--- a/libgcc/unwind-dw2-fde-dip.c
+++ b/libgcc/unwind-dw2-fde-dip.c
@@ -200,7 +200,11 @@
 
   struct ext_dl_phdr_info
     {
+#if defined __FRV_FDPIC__ || defined __BFIN_FDPIC__
+      struct elf32_fdpic_loadaddr dlpi_addr;
+#else
       ElfW(Addr) dlpi_addr;
+#endif
       const char *dlpi_name;
       const ElfW(Phdr) *dlpi_phdr;
       ElfW(Half) dlpi_phnum;
